            <div xml:id="d144">

                <pb facs="0258" n="140" xml:id="pg140"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">314.115C43/131: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        Guatemala</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Geissler</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-07-03T11:00:00-04:00">July 3, 1929—11
                    a.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>36. Your telegram No. 85, July 1. Shufeldt advises Department he. is prepared to
                    submit documentary evidence in support of claim totaling $500,000, but in order
                    to obtain prompt settlement and avoid further losses will consider smaller
                    amount provided payment is in cash. So inform Foreign Minister whether or not
                    Davidson has left. If Davidson has not left inform him confidentially these
                    instructions and advise him that if Government of Guatemala is prepared to enter
                    negotiations on basis of prompt cash settlement he may close with them for a
                    minimum of $150,000.</p>
                <p>Telegraph results.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
